-- title:
--   Finite edge-chart cover over an open of the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient
-- statement:
--   The hypotheses fall into seven groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic base.** A prime $r$; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an element $\pi$ which is irreducible (`hπ`), with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology (`hcomplete`), residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next a characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $Onr$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally a homomorphism $v\!\det:\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) which, by `hvdet`, satisfies $v\!\det(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Group data.** A group $G$, a homomorphism $\sigma:G\to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma\le G$ containing an element whose image under $\sigma$ is a scalar matrix with $v\!\det=2$ (`hcent`) and an element with $v\!\det\circ\sigma$ equal to $1$ (`hodd`); a subgroup $\Gamma'$ characterised by `hΓ'` as the set of $x\in\Gamma$ with $v\!\det(\sigma x)$ even. A homomorphism $\rho:G\to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ which is $\sigma$ followed by the projection (`hρ`), such that the stabiliser in $\rho(\Gamma')$ of every vertex of the lattice tree over $(\mathcal O,K_0)$ (a homothety class of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$) is finite (`hdisc`), and such that finitely many vertices meet every $\rho(\Gamma')$-orbit (`hcocpt`).
--
--   **The curve and the uniformisation functor.** A scheme $\mathcal X$ and a proper flat morphism $f:\mathcal X\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; a family $\Theta$ assigning, to every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $Onr\to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ (an assignment $M\mapsto \mathrm{line}(M)\subseteq B\otimes_{\mathcal O}M$ of submodules of the base changes of full lattices, with invertible quotients, monotone, equivariant for scalar matrices, and non-degenerate at every prime) to $B$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$. It is assumed natural in $B$ (`hΘnat`); invariant under the twisted $\Gamma$-action, i.e. $\Theta$ takes the same value on $x$ and $x'$ whenever $x'_1=x_1\circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$-pullback of $x_2$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma$ (`hΘinv`); for algebraically closed fields $k$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\psi:Onr\to k$, surjective onto $k$-points with fibres exactly the twisted $\Gamma$-orbits (`hΘfib`); and initial among such natural invariant families, the factorisation being unique (`hΘuniv`, summarised here).
--
--   **Analytic frame.** A field $C$ over $K_0$, complete and algebraically closed, valued in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$; a commutative ring $R$ with compatible $\mathcal O$- and $C$-algebra structures; a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi$ of $K_0$ in $C$ (an element of $K_0$ whose value lies strictly between $0$ and $1$ and whose powers scale all values of $K_0$); and `hF`, the assertion that $(\pi,\varpi,R)$ is an adic frame: $\pi$ is irreducible, $R\to C$ is injective with image the set of elements of value $\le 1$, $R$ is $\pi$-adically complete, $\mathcal O$ is the set of elements of $K_0$ of value $\le 1$, the image of $K_0$ in $C$ is closed, and $\pi$ and $\varpi$ have the same image in $C$. Further: an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\psi_0:Onr\to R$; `hrk`, that for $x$ with $v(x)<1$ and $y\neq 0$ some power $v(x)^n$ is $\le v(y)$; `hval`, that every nonzero $\varepsilon\in\Gamma_0$ dominates the value of some nonzero element of $C$; `hex`, that every point of the Drinfeld upper half plane $C\setminus K_0$ lies in one of the affinoids of $\varpi$; and the assumption that the ring of functions holomorphic on all these affinoids is a domain.
--
--   **The uniformisation of adic points.** A map $\Phi$ from adic points (compatible systems of Deligne data over the rings $R/\pi^{n+1}$) to $R$-points of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} R$, with `hΦ` asserting four things: the reduction of $\Phi(x)$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(R/\pi^{n+1})$ is $\Theta$ applied to the pair consisting of $\psi_0$ reduced mod $\pi^{n+1}$ and the $n$-th component of $x$; $\Phi$ is surjective; $\Phi(x)=\Phi(x')$ if and only if $x'=x\cdot\sigma\gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma'$; and restriction along $R\to C$ is injective on $R$-points and hits every $C$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} C$.
--
--   **Chart data.** An element $g_1\in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ with matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ (`hg₁`); the structure morphisms $s_n:\operatorname{Spec}(Onr/\pi^{n+1})\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ induced by the algebra map (`hsn`); and morphisms $\kappa_{h,n}:\operatorname{Spec} A_n\to \mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}(Onr/\pi^{n+1})$, where $A_n$ is the reduction mod $\pi^{n+1}$ of the edge chart ring `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` (the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPoly}_2(Onr)/(\text{edge relation})$ away from the edge discriminant). The hypothesis `hκ` is the chart compatibility clause: for all $h$, $n$, every $\mathcal O$- and $Onr$-algebra $B$ in a tower with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $Onr$-algebra homomorphism $\bar x:A_n\to B$ and all Deligne data $d,P$ over $B$, if $d$ has line at the standard lattice equal to the span of $\bar x(\xi)\otimes e_0+1\otimes e_1$, line at $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ equal to the image of the span of $1\otimes e_0+\bar x(\eta)\otimes e_1$ under the base-changed action of $g_1$, and $d$ is non-degenerate at every prime relative to the pair $(g_1\cdot \text{std},\text{std})$ (`InEdgeChart`), and if $P$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$, then the $\mathcal X$-point $\Theta(\,\mathrm{tower\ map},P)$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\bar x$ followed by $\kappa_{h,n}$ followed by the first projection of the pullback.
--
--   Finally, an element $h\in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and an open subscheme $V$ of $\mathcal X$ are given.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There is a finite subset $T$ of the edge chart ring `chartERing Onr (algebraMap 𝒪 Onr π) r` such that:
--
--   (i) for every $t\in T$ and every $n\in\mathbb N$, the basic open $D(\bar t)$ of $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$ determined by the image of $t$ is contained in the preimage of $V$ under $\kappa_{h,n}$ followed by the first projection $\mathcal X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O}\operatorname{Spec}(Onr/\pi^{n+1})\to\mathcal X$; and
--
--   (ii) for every adic point $x$ and every $z\in C$ with $z=x.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C$, if $z$ lies in the union of the vertex tube of the image of $h$ in $\mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$, the edge tube of that image, and the vertex tube of the image of $h\cdot\mathrm{edgeFlip}$ (where $\mathrm{edgeFlip}=\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,1)$), and if the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ is carried into $V$ by $\Phi(x)$, then some $t\in T$ satisfies: $z$ lies in $C\setminus K_0$, and for every adic point $x'$ with $x'.\mathrm{toOmega}\,C=z$ and every $n\in\mathbb N$ there exist a ring homomorphism $\bar x:A_n\to R/\pi^{n+1}$ and a Deligne datum $d$ over $R/\pi^{n+1}$ such that $\bar x$ composed with $Onr\to A_n$ is $\psi_0$ followed by reduction mod $\pi^{n+1}$; $d$ has line at the standard lattice equal to the span of $\bar x(\xi)\otimes e_0+1\otimes e_1$ and line at $g_1\cdot(\text{standard lattice})$ equal to the image under the base-changed action of $g_1$ of the span of $1\otimes e_0+\bar x(\eta)\otimes e_1$, and $d$ is non-degenerate at every prime relative to $(g_1\cdot\text{std},\text{std})$; the $n$-th component of $x'$ is the $h^{-1}$-pullback of $d$; and $\bar x(\bar t)$ is a unit of $R/\pi^{n+1}$.
--
--   This is the finiteness step in the comparison of the $p$-adic analytic uniformisation of a Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient with sections of the algebraic curve: the points of the closed edge region attached to $h$ whose image under $\Phi$ factors through a given open $V$ are covered by finitely many basic opens of the edge chart ring, the chart coordinates of such a point being invertible at one of the chosen elements. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_linearPieces_le_preimage_holOn_apply_toOmega_eq_of_cerednikDrinfeld_quotient), where sections over $V$ are turned into holomorphic functions on the tubes.
